# Intent: no music for 4.5 s pauses the unit's own dance (was 9 s) and clear music takes it right back to the mood it was in (owner 2026-11-13: "cut that 9 seconds in half and if the music picks up then go right back to the mood you were in, fast, medium or slow"). The session machine remembers whether the pause came from the dance or the slow mood and the glue starts the sway again at once, with the block timers moved on by the pause. The host does the same (bot 0.2.80).
# Upstream: MaiPai only (hal_music.cpp, maipai_music_judge.h). Applies after 126.
# Check after a flash: with Home stopped, music, stop it for 5 s (the dance stops), start it again (the dance is back at once, the same mood).
diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/hal_music.cpp b/firmware/main/hal/hal_music.cpp
--- a/firmware/main/hal/hal_music.cpp
+++ b/firmware/main/hal/hal_music.cpp
@@ -161,6 +161,10 @@
     } else if (action == MMJ_ACTION_BREAK) {
         // The slow mood between dance blocks (owner 2026-11-13: "not just not dance"): the gentle sway goes on with
         // one note until the next full dance.
+        if (!dancing && (charging || battery >= 40)) {  // back from a pause into the slow mood: the gentle sway again
+            maipai_music_dance_start();
+            dancing = true;
+        }
         offline_music_notes(dancing ? 1 : 0);
         ESP_LOGI("HAL-Music", "offline music: slow mood");
     } else if (action == MMJ_ACTION_PAUSE) {
